# M4.29.2 Agent start failure — shared log directory mode

Date: 2026-08-28

## Symptom

The eight committed artifacts were installed with exact expected hashes and
systemd was reloaded. On the first authorized start,
`tu1nz_agentmode.service` did not produce its external observation within the
60-second gate. The maintenance error trap stopped Agentmode, Integrity and
Monitor.

Journal evidence:

`install: cannot change permissions of /var/log/tausendunde1nz/health: Operation not permitted`

## Cause

The observer used `install -d -m 0750` on every cycle for both its dedicated
state path and the pre-existing shared health-log directory. The shared log
directory intentionally has an existing setgid group mode. Reapplying a
different mode is unnecessary and was denied inside the hardened service
sandbox.

## Impact

- Control mutation by the new service: none;
- observation/runtime state: not created by the failed start;
- Integrity/Monitor restart: not reached;
- Adult Candidate: untouched and never started;
- affected services after the trap: stopped/inactive;
- installed bytes: first M4.29.2 commit remains installed but inactive.

## Remediation

Runtime directories are created and permissioned once by the authorized
installer. Runtime scripts use `mkdir -p` only, which does not alter existing
directory modes. New test directories still inherit the scripts' `0027` umask
and become `0750`. Rebind hashes, commit, push and pass CI before reinstalling.
